  "description": "DISHAQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C52 H57 Dy4 N20 O19 3+,3(Cl1 O4 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.518-3.618 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.32-101.44°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C52H69Cl3N20O37Dy4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
